.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.WORKSPACE.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.workspace.mk
.Nd workspace role: builds every framework and aggregates their output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fd .include <mk.workspace.mk>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A workspace is the top of a source tree.
Any immediate subdirectory whose makefile sets
.Va PREREQS
is a framework; they are found without being listed and built in
.Va PREREQS
order.
A framework whose prerequisite failed is skipped, not built, and counts as failed.
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "BUILD_REPORT_DIR"
.It Va PARENT_WS
Absolute paths of parent workspaces, searched in order for frameworks and
hook files not found here.
A path that does not exist is a warning.
.It Va BUILD_REPORT_DIR
Where
.Cm all Va REPORT=yes
writes its dashboard.
Default
.Pa build-report .
.It Va TEST_REPORT_DIR
The same for
.Cm test .
Default
.Pa test-report .
.It Va WS_DOCS_DIR
Where
.Cm docs
writes the workspace page.
Default
.Pa build/docs .
.It Va DOCS_DIR , Va DOC_PROJECT_NAME , Va DOC_PROJECT_BRIEF
See
.Xr mk.docs.mk 5 .
.It Va FW
With
.Cm test :
only this framework.
.It Va WS
With
.Cm add-parent :
the path to add.
.It Va DESTDIR , Va PREFIX
With
.Cm install .
.Va PREFIX
defaults to
.Pa /usr/local .
.El
.Pp
.Va REPORT , FAIL_FAST , RUN_ID , SANITIZE
and the target selection are described in
.Xr mk.common.mk 5
and forwarded to every framework.
.Ss Targets
.Bl -tag -width "add-parent"
.It Cm all
Build every framework, then copy their
.Pa bin , lib
and
.Pa share
into this workspace's
.Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY .
This is the default.
.It Cm test
Run every framework's tests; see
.Xr mk.test.mk 5 .
.It Cm docs
Document every framework, in
.Va PREREQS
order, and write a landing page.
.It Cm clean
Remove the current target key's output and reports.
With
.Va TARGET=all ,
every key's.
.It Cm install
Copy the built
.Pa bin , lib
and
.Pa share
into
.Va DESTDIR Ns Va PREFIX .
It does not build first.
.It Cm add-parent
Append
.Va WS
to
.Va PARENT_WS
in the makefile.
.It Cm help
Print the current selection and the usual variables.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "build-report/RUN_ID/KEY/"
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /
aggregated output
.It Pa .gen-fw-order.mk
the framework order, generated
.It Pa build-report/ Ns Ar RUN_ID Ns Pa / Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /
build dashboard
.It Pa test-report/ Ns Ar RUN_ID Ns Pa / Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /
test dashboard
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Non-zero if any framework failed or was skipped for a failed prerequisite, even
when the run went on past it; a summary names each one.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PARENT_WS=/work/base-ws
\&.include <mk.workspace.mk>
.Ed
.Pp
.Dl $ bmake install DESTDIR=/tmp/stage PREFIX=/opt/demo
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It framework build order could not be determined
.Pa scripts/gen-fw-order.sh
failed; its reason is printed above this line.
.El
.Sh CAVEATS
The packaging targets
.Cm pkg , deb , rpm , msi
and
.Cm port
are designed but not implemented.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.docs.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.local.mk 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
